// Regla Sigma: proc_creation_win_configsecuritypolicy_download_file.yml
// ID Sigma: 1f0f6176-6482-4027-b151-00071af39d7e
// Título: Arbitrary File Download Via ConfigSecurityPolicy.EXE
// Descripción: Detects the execution of "ConfigSecurityPolicy.EXE", a binary part of Windows Defender used to manage settings in Windows Defender.
Users can configure different pilot collections for each of the co-management workloads.
It can be abused by attackers in order to upload or download files.

// Fecha de creación: 2021-11-26
// Fecha de modificación: 2022-05-16
// Aplica a: Producto: windows | Categoría: process_creation
// Producto: windows
// Categoría: process_creation
// Servicio: 
// Nivel: medium
// Pipeline: microsoft_xdr
// Ruta original: C:\SigmaLab\sigma\rules\windows\process_creation\proc_creation_win_configsecuritypolicy_download_file.yml
// Requiere validación en el entorno de destino.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "ConfigSecurityPolicy.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\ConfigSecurityPolicy.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "ConfigSecurityPolicy.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "ftp://" or ProcessCommandLine contains "http://" or ProcessCommandLine contains "https://")
